Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work on any
                      number of Instances solely for your own internal
                      operations, using only the Community Capabilities defined
                      below, provided that each Instance contains no more than
                      five User Accounts, three Projects and 250 Bugs, subject
                      to the continued-use permission below. These conditions
                      apply together.

                      "Community Capabilities" means core bug tracking, project
                      management including the Pulse boards, basic GitHub
                      integration, and data export, together with the account
                      administration, authentication, storage, backup,
                      restoration and other supporting operations needed to use
                      those capabilities. It excludes the reserved production
                      capabilities listed below, except to the limited extent
                      expressly permitted by the continued-use paragraph. This
                      definition and the reserved list are fixed for this
                      version, not by a future pricing page or a change to a
                      feature flag.

                      Reserved production capabilities are AI insights,
                      duplicate detection and other AI analysis; reporting
                      beyond the included Pulse views and Friday brief; custom
                      fields and workflows; third-party REST API integrations
                      other than the included basic GitHub integration and data
                      export; scheduled email reports; advanced GitHub
                      integration; S3 attachment storage; SAML single sign-on;
                      audit logging and audit-log export; advanced permissions;
                      SLA management; private LLM integration; child-licence
                      issuance; and the supplied white-label and custom-branding
                      management features. This reservation of supplied branding
                      features does not prohibit modifying names, logos or
                      styles in a build otherwise used within this grant,
                      subject to required notices and applicable trademark
                      rights. Internal API calls needed for Community
                      Capabilities are not reserved third-party REST API
                      integrations.

                      Your employees and contractors may use an Instance on your
                      behalf for your internal operations, within the same
                      account limits. This grant does not permit you to provide
                      the Licensed Work as a hosted or managed service to third
                      parties, whether paid or free, or operate Instances for
                      clients' own operations. Such production use, use of
                      reserved capabilities, or use beyond the numerical limits
                      requires a separate commercial licence authorising that
                      scope of use. Mere redistribution remains governed by the
                      Terms below.

                      An "Instance" is one production deployment using one
                      logical application datastore, including a SQL database or
                      a CSV storage directory. Application processes, servers or
                      containers sharing that datastore form one Instance.
                      Replicas used solely for the same deployment's replication
                      or failover do not form additional Instances. A separately
                      operated production deployment using an independent
                      datastore is a separate Instance.

                      A "User Account" is each account record that exists in the
                      Instance, including administrator and service accounts,
                      whether or not recently used. A "Project" is each project
                      record that exists in the Instance. A "Bug" is each bug
                      record that exists in the Instance, regardless of status.
                      A record ceases to count when deleted from the operational
                      datastore. Counts are totals across the Instance, not per
                      person, organisation, project or application process.

                      After a commercial licence expires or its authorised scope
                      decreases, you may continue to retain, view, edit, export
                      and delete records lawfully created while that
                      authorisation was in effect, including associated data in
                      reserved features, even if the Instance exceeds the
                      numerical limits. This limited permission also applies to
                      existing client data on formerly authorised hosted
                      Instances; it does not permit onboarding new hosted
                      customers or using other reserved capabilities to generate
                      new results. You may create further User Accounts,
                      Projects or Bugs for your own internal operations only
                      where the total for the corresponding record type
                      immediately after creation does not exceed the limit
                      above. An excess in another record type does not prevent
                      such creation. This permission does not authorise use of
                      separately licensed software or services.

                      A disaster-recovery standby maintained solely for
                      replication, backup or recovery testing, and serving no
                      live operational workload, does not count as a production
                      Instance. When it takes over the same workload in place of
                      the failed deployment, it replaces that Instance.
                      Simultaneous independent production operation counts as
                      another Instance.

                      These permissions apply equally to the original Licensed
                      Work and modified versions. Changing or removing a
                      technical check does not expand the scope of production
                      use permitted by this grant. This grant imposes no
                      additional conditions on the rights to copy, modify,
                      redistribute or make non-production use provided by the
                      Terms below, or on rights available under applicable law.

